{
  "question": 2,
  "title": "Q2 Log-squared integral",
  "subject": "Math",
  "modules": [
    {
      "id": "q2-sol",
      "moduleId": "solution-steps",
      "title": "Worked solution",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 0,
      "width": 560,
      "height": 764,
      "anchorMode": "board-fixed-size",
      "solution": {
        "version": 1,
        "title": "Q2 · ∫ ln²x / (x² + 2x + 4)",
        "problem": "Evaluate $I=\\int_0^\\infty \\dfrac{(\\ln x)^2}{x^2+2x+4}\\,dx$ exactly.",
        "steps": [
          {
            "id": "q2-sol-s01",
            "math": "(2t)^2+2(2t)+4 = 4(t^2+t+1)",
            "note": "Substitute x = 2t, so dx = 2 dt and the quadratic becomes 4(t² + t + 1)."
          },
          {
            "id": "q2-sol-s02",
            "math": "\\int_0^{\\infty}\\frac{(\\ln x)^2}{x^2+2x+4}\\,dx = \\frac12\\int_0^{\\infty}\\frac{(\\ln 2+\\ln t)^2}{t^2+t+1}\\,dt",
            "note": "After the substitution; expand (ln 2 + ln t)² = ln²2 + 2 ln 2 · ln t + ln²t, giving J₀, J₁, J₂."
          },
          {
            "id": "q2-sol-s03",
            "math": "\\frac{d}{dt}\\left(\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{3}}\\arctan\\frac{2t+1}{\\sqrt{3}}\\right) = \\frac{1}{t^2+t+1}",
            "note": "Antiderivative for J₀."
          },
          {
            "id": "q2-sol-s04",
            "math": "\\int_0^{\\infty}\\frac{1}{t^2+t+1}\\,dt = \\frac{2}{\\sqrt3}\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{2}-\\frac{\\pi}{6}\\right) = \\frac{2\\pi}{3\\sqrt{3}}",
            "note": "J₀ from the arctan antiderivative."
          },
          {
            "id": "q2-sol-s05",
            "math": "\\int_0^{\\infty}\\frac{\\ln t}{t^2+t+1}\\,dt = 0",
            "note": "J₁ = 0: t ↦ 1/t maps the integrand to its negative because t² + t + 1 is palindromic (see the graph)."
          },
          {
            "id": "q2-sol-s06",
            "math": "\\int_0^{\\infty}\\frac{t^{0.5-1}}{t^2+t+1}\\,dt = \\frac{\\pi\\sin(0.5\\pi/3)}{\\sin(\\pi/3)\\sin(0.5\\pi)}",
            "note": "Mellin transform F(s) = ∫t^(s−1)/(t² + t + 1) dt = π sin((1 − s)π/3)/(sin(π/3) sin πs) for 0 < s < 2, so J_k = F⁽ᵏ⁾(1). Spot-check at s = 1/2."
          },
          {
            "id": "q2-sol-s07",
            "math": "\\frac{\\pi}{\\sin(\\pi/3)}\\cdot\\frac{\\sin(0.01\\pi/3)}{\\sin(0.01\\pi)} \\approx \\frac{2\\pi}{\\sqrt3}\\left(\\frac13+\\frac{4\\pi^2}{81}(0.01)^2\\right)",
            "note": "With s = 1 + ε, F = (π/sin(π/3))·sin(πε/3)/sin(πε) = (2π/√3)(1/3 + 4π²ε²/81 + …). Spot-check of the expansion at ε = 0.01."
          },
          {
            "id": "q2-sol-s08",
            "math": "2\\cdot\\frac{2\\pi}{\\sqrt3}\\cdot\\frac{4\\pi^2}{81} = \\frac{16\\pi^3}{81\\sqrt3}",
            "note": "J₂ = F″(1) = 2 × (coefficient of ε²)."
          },
          {
            "id": "q2-sol-s09",
            "math": "\\int_0^{\\infty}\\frac{(\\ln t)^2}{t^2+t+1}\\,dt = \\frac{16\\pi^3}{81\\sqrt{3}}",
            "note": "Numerical check of J₂."
          },
          {
            "id": "q2-sol-s10",
            "math": "\\frac12\\left((\\ln 2)^2\\cdot\\frac{2\\pi}{3\\sqrt3}+0+\\frac{16\\pi^3}{81\\sqrt3}\\right) = \\frac{\\pi(\\ln 2)^2}{3\\sqrt3}+\\frac{8\\pi^3}{81\\sqrt3}",
            "note": "Assemble I = ½(ln²2 · J₀ + 2 ln 2 · J₁ + J₂)."
          },
          {
            "id": "q2-sol-s11",
            "math": "= \\frac{\\sqrt3\\,\\pi\\left(27(\\ln 2)^2+8\\pi^2\\right)}{243}",
            "note": "Single fraction."
          },
          {
            "id": "q2-sol-s12",
            "math": "\\frac{\\sqrt3\\,\\pi\\left(27(\\ln 2)^2+8\\pi^2\\right)}{243} \\approx 2.05853",
            "note": "Decimal value."
          },
          {
            "id": "q2-sol-s13",
            "math": "\\int_0^{\\infty}\\frac{(\\ln x)^2}{x^2+2x+4}\\,dx \\approx 2.05853",
            "note": "Final check against direct quadrature."
          }
        ],
        "answer": "I=\\dfrac{\\pi\\ln^2 2}{3\\sqrt3}+\\dfrac{8\\pi^3}{81\\sqrt3}=\\dfrac{\\sqrt3\\,\\pi\\left(27\\ln^2 2+8\\pi^2\\right)}{243}\\approx 2.05853",
        "source": {
          "kind": "manual"
        }
      }
    },
